  «text (0,6600) 1.6 7 1 0x1000000 -1 -1 "ï»¿CONTROLLER - shuffler_ctrl_dll2.dll: the firmware control stack (6_RTOS/ctrl_core) as a QSPICE C-block"Â»
  «text (0,6200) 1 7 1 0x1000000 -1 -1 "ï»¿The DLL models the INA239 / hall sampling and quantisation, the 10 kHz control tick and the gain matrix M from params.h (MSEL = 0),"Â»
  «text (0,6000) 1 7 1 0x1000000 -1 -1 "ï»¿the 100 kHz S9i M (MSEL = 1) or ctrl_M2.txt (MSEL = 2). shuffler_ctrl_dll2.dll and ctrl_M2.txt must sit next to the top sheet."Â»
  «text (0,5800) 1 7 1 0x1000000 -1 -1 "ï»¿Open loop until TEN (CTRL_EN low: the duties D0A1 .. D0B2), closed loop after. Every test input of the DLL is a .param on the top sheet."Â»
  «text (0,5600) 1 7 1 0x1000000 -1 -1 "ï»¿Inputs: PV1P / PV2P / PV3P = the string nodes the INA239s see, HS_* = hall outputs of the shufflers. Outputs: one PWM pair per leg."Â»
  «text (0,5400) 1 7 1 0x1000000 -1 -1 "ï»¿Signal flow left to right: sources -> DLL -> duty override (duty() .func) -> PWM_Modulator XP1 (converter 1) and XP2 (converter 2)."Â»
  «text (0,4900) 1.2 7 1 0x1000000 -1 -1 "ï»¿ENABLE, REFERENCE STEPS AND PWM RAMPS"Â»
